{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Declare-a-System","type":"heading","text":"Declare a System"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@System","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for you: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"reference"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","type":"heading","text":"Run Systems in a Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" require one system to run after or before another; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" skips"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},{"type":"text","text":" finds those pairs so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test can keep a schedule free of them. To learn more, see "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters","title":"System Parameters"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"],"anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","title":"Building and Running Schedules"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","title":"Main-Actor Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"],"anchor":"Built-In-Systems","title":"Built-In Systems"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"],"anchor":"Profiling","title":"Profiling"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"externalID":"Systems","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Systems","symbolKind":"module"},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs them."}],"kind":"article","title":"Scheduling Systems","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","role":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"EventWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventWriter","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Declaring Systems","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"type":"topic","title":"Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduleBuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"text":"’s closure.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"System()","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemProfile"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","title":"Driving a World from an App","type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","abstract":[{"text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it read results and take part in a step.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world."}],"required":true,"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"run"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"inout"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"World","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"run(in:)","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"title":"Query","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that reads a resource.","type":"text"}],"title":"ResourceReader","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceReader","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"title":"EventReader","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemParameter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemParameter"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemParameter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Ambiguity","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Update","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Update","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","role":"symbol","title":"ForwardChanges","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardChanges","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MainActorSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MainActorSystem"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SystemTiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"System","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"access","defaultImplementations":1,"required":true,"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Access"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScheduledSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduledSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"type":"topic","title":"RemovedComponents","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ambiguities","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"ambiguities()","abstract":[{"text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orders.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"title":"UpdateEvents","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","abstract":[{"text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has had its chance to read them.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ForwardEvents","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule can await the events."}],"title":"ForwardEvents","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Schedule","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SystemSet"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"title":"ResourceWriter","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceWriter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}]}}}